# `if ((type as TypeReference).node)` in a loop: a store by name appends the field, most objects are without it. The look at the slot parts three ways:
# filled: the typed run . EMPTY, and the object's own byte and the guard of the class say that nothing stands above and nothing lies outside the slots: the read is undefined and goes on in the typed way . else the closed arm.
# f1 = use, f2 = flagsOf, f3 = levelOf, f4 = useEach, f5 = flagsOfEach, f6 = levelOfEach.
# Outside of loops: empty-slot-of-a-field-that-a-store-appends-is-a-case-of-its-own.ir. A field of the birth (`flags`) gets no such side: its slot is never empty.
# `level: Level` lies in four bytes with marks for absent, undefined and null, and its look asks for a number: it fails on all three, so its failing side is no empty slot: null there is read as null.
# RUN: walk f4 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f4:Body
# CHECK: [[filled]]: boolean @Boolean = IsSlotFilled {{*}}key="part"
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch [[filled]] -> taken {{*}}, notTaken [[empty]]()
# CHECK: [[empty]]() isInLoop=true:
# CHECK-NEXT: = HasNoFieldOutsideSlot
# CHECK: = AreMembersUnchanged {{*}}key="part"
# RUN(BIRTH): walk f5 mechanisms=all
# BIRTH-LABEL: code f5:Body
# BIRTH-NOT: = AreMembersUnchanged
# RUN(RAW): walk f6 mechanisms=all
# RAW-LABEL: code f6:Body
# RAW-NOT: = AreMembersUnchanged
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
